<h1 class=3D"sectionedit1" id=3D"bbcode_plugin">BBCode Plugin</h1>
<div class=3D"level1">

</div>

<h2 class=3D"sectionedit2" id=3D"general">General</h2>
<div class=3D"level2">

<p>
BBCode is a simple-to-understand markup language. See: <a href=3D"https://e=
n.wikipedia.org/wiki/BBCode" class=3D"interwiki iw_wp" title=3D"https://en.=
wikipedia.org/wiki/BBCode">BBCode</a>
</p>

<p>
The plugin provides a variety of different elements, called tags. For examp=
le, there are tags for headlines, text formattings, links, images, and so o=
n.
</p>

<p>
Many tags have attributes that modify the behaviour of the tag (such as the=
 "width" and "height" attribute of images that define the dimensions the im=
age is displayed with). Attribute values are set in double quotes: [tag att=
ribute=3D"value"]<br>

<em>(In fact, if the value does not contain blanks, you could go without th=
e quotes - we recommend always to use them.)</em>
</p>

</div>

<h2 class=3D"sectionedit3" id=3D"available_tags">Available Tags</h2>
<div class=3D"level2">

</div>

<h3 class=3D"sectionedit4" id=3D"content_elements">Content elements</h3>
<div class=3D"level3">
<div class=3D"wrap_right wrap_round wrap_tip plugin_wrap" style=3D"width: 2=
00px; max-width: 100%;">
<p>
It's not too complicated to add custom BBCode tags - <a href=3D"https://wik=
i.flatpress.org/doc:plugins:bbcode:tips" class=3D"wikilink1" title=3D"doc:p=
lugins:bbcode:tips" data-wiki-id=3D"doc:plugins:bbcode:tips">here's how</a>=
.
</p>
</div><ul>
<li class=3D"level1"><div class=3D"li"> [h2]Heading 2nd level[/h2] to [h6]H=
eading 6th level[/h6]<br>
<em>(Because h1 is the heading for the page title, it has been disabled in =
the content of every page.)</em></div>
</li>
<li class=3D"level1"><div class=3D"li"> [quote]text quotation[/quote]</div>
</li>
<li class=3D"level1"><div class=3D"li"> [code]code[/code]</div>
</li>
<li class=3D"level1"><div class=3D"li"> [list]<br>
[*]bulleted list element 1<br>
[*]bulleted list element 2<br>
[/list]</div>
</li>
<li class=3D"level1"><div class=3D"li"> [list=3D#]<br>
[*]Numbered list element 1<br>
[*]Numbered list element 2<br>
[/list]</div>
</li>
<li class=3D"level1"><div class=3D"li"> [html][/html] literal html. All cod=
e between these is not changed.<br>
<em>Alternative: Enable <a href=3D"https://wiki.flatpress.org/doc:plugins:b=
bcode:tips" class=3D"wikilink1" title=3D"doc:plugins:bbcode:tips" data-wiki=
-id=3D"doc:plugins:bbcode:tips">inline HTML</a>.</em></div>
</li>
</ul>

</div>

<h3 class=3D"sectionedit7" id=3D"text_formatting">Text formatting</h3>
<div class=3D"level3">
<ul>
<li class=3D"level1"><div class=3D"li"> [b]bold[/b]</div>
</li>
<li class=3D"level1"><div class=3D"li"> [i]italic[/i]</div>
</li>
<li class=3D"level1"><div class=3D"li"> [u]underlined[/u]</div>
</li>
<li class=3D"level1"><div class=3D"li"> [del]strike-through[/del]</div>
</li>
<li class=3D"level1"><div class=3D"li"> [size=3D"80%"]smaller[/size] or [si=
ze=3D"120%"]bigger[/size] text</div>
</li>
<li class=3D"level1"><div class=3D"li"> [font=3D"FONT"]font[/font]<br>
<em>FONT is a valid css font-family value ("sans-serif", "Times" etc.)</em>=
</div>
</li>
<li class=3D"level1 node"><div class=3D"li"> [color=3D"COLOR"]color[/color]=
<br>
<em>COLOR is a valid css color value (e.g. #cb0600)</em>  </div>
<ul>
<li class=3D"level2"><div class=3D"li"> Example color picker to get the cod=
es at <a href=3D"https://www.w3schools.com/colors/colors_picker.asp" class=
=3D"urlextern" title=3D"https://www.w3schools.com/colors/colors_picker.asp"=
 rel=3D"ugc nofollow">W3schools</a></div>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>

</div>

<h3 class=3D"sectionedit8" id=3D"links">Links</h3>
<div class=3D"level3">
<ul>
<li class=3D"level1"><div class=3D"li"> Simple: [url]DESTINATION[/url]</div=
>
</li>
<li class=3D"level1 node"><div class=3D"li"> Advanced: [url=3D"DESTINATION"=
 (rel=3D"relationship") (target=3D"target")]Link text[/url] <br>
<em>(items in parenthesis are optional, when you use those items you have t=
o leave away the parenthesis!)</em>.</div>
<ul>
<li class=3D"level2 node"><div class=3D"li"> <strong>DESTINATION</strong> m=
ay be:</div>
<ul>
<li class=3D"level3"><div class=3D"li"> an external <abbr title=3D"Uniform =
Resource Locator">URL</abbr>: "https://www.example.org"</div>
</li>
<li class=3D"level3"><div class=3D"li"> an uploaded file: "attachs/somefile=
.zip"</div>
</li>
<li class=3D"level3"><div class=3D"li"> an uploaded file: "images/someimage=
.jpg"</div>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li class=3D"level2"><div class=3D"li"> <strong>rel</strong> specifies the =
relationship between the current and the linked document (see <a href=3D"ht=
tps://www.w3schools.com/TAGS/att_a_rel.asp" class=3D"urlextern" title=3D"ht=
tps://www.w3schools.com/TAGS/att_a_rel.asp" rel=3D"ugc nofollow">doc on W3S=
chools</a>)</div>
</li>
<li class=3D"level2"><div class=3D"li"> <strong>target</strong> (available =
as of FlatPress 1.3) specifies where to open the linked document (see <a hr=
ef=3D"https://www.w3schools.com/TAGS/att_a_target.asp" class=3D"urlextern" =
title=3D"https://www.w3schools.com/TAGS/att_a_target.asp" rel=3D"ugc nofoll=
ow">doc on W3Schools</a>)</div>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li class=3D"level1"><div class=3D"li"> Simple email link: [mail]user@examp=
le.org[/mail]</div>
</li>
<li class=3D"level1"><div class=3D"li"> Advanced email link: [mail=3D"user@=
example.org"]link text[/url]</div>
</li>
</ul>

</div>

<h3 class=3D"sectionedit9" id=3D"images">Images</h3>
<div class=3D"level3">
<ul>
<li class=3D"level1 node"><div class=3D"li"> [img=3D"IMAGEPATH" (alt=3D"alt=
ernate text") (title=3D"title text") (popup=3D"false") (scale=3D"NN%") (wid=
th=3D"N") (height=3D"N") (float=3D"left"|"right") (loading=3D"lazy"|"eager"=
)] <br>
<em>(items in parenthesis are optional, when you use those items you have t=
o leave away the parenthesis!)</em>.</div>
<ul>
<li class=3D"level2"><div class=3D"li"> if <strong>IMAGEPATH</strong> begin=
s with images/ it will be automatically translated into the appropriate <ab=
br title=3D"Uniform Resource Locator">URL</abbr> for fp-content/images/</di=
v>
</li>
<li class=3D"level2"><div class=3D"li"> <strong>alt</strong> sets the alter=
nate text</div>
</li>
<li class=3D"level2"><div class=3D"li"> <strong>title</strong>: title shown=
 on mouse-over.</div>
</li>
<li class=3D"level2"><div class=3D"li"> <strong>popup</strong> If set to tr=
ue and the <em>LightBox2</em> plug-in is enabled (it is by default) display=
 of the image will driven by the plug-in. (Actually the plug-in is the Ligh=
tBox work-alike <a href=3D"http://www.digitalia.be/software/slimbox" class=
=3D"urlextern" title=3D"http://www.digitalia.be/software/slimbox" rel=3D"ug=
c nofollow">Slimbox</a>).</div>
</li>
<li class=3D"level2 node"><div class=3D"li"> <strong>scale</strong> creates=
 a thumbnail NN% smaller than the original. Example: [img=3Dimages/picture.=
jpg scale=3D5%]</div>
<ul>
<li class=3D"level4"><div class=3D"li"> If the <em>thumb</em> plugin is ena=
bled (it is by default) and the server has the GD2 php extension installed =
(usually it is) the generated thumbnail is a real, static thumbnail. Otherw=
ise the image will look small in browser but the browser will be actually d=
ownloading the original file.</div>
</li>
<li class=3D"level4"><div class=3D"li"> Setting a scale value automatically=
 invokes popup=3Dtrue and clicking on the thumbnail will display the image =
in a "LightBox".</div>
</li>
<li class=3D"level4"><div class=3D"li"> Scale doesn't work on remote images=
.</div>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li class=3D"level2 node"><div class=3D"li"> <strong>width</strong> and <st=
rong>height</strong> set the width or height on the image in pixels. You ca=
n use both of them or only one. If you set only one the re-sized image will=
 retain its aspect ratio.</div>
<ul>
<li class=3D"level3"><div class=3D"li"> if the <em>thumb</em> plug-in is en=
abled and the GD2 php extension is installed on the server (usually it is) =
it will generate a thumbnail image file and popup=3Dtrue will be invoked, u=
nless specifically set to false.</div>
</li>
<li class=3D"level3"><div class=3D"li"> Static thumbnail creation does not =
work on remote images.</div>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li class=3D"level2"><div class=3D"li"> <strong>float</strong> float the im=
ages to the left or to the right</div>
</li>
<li class=3D"level2"><div class=3D"li"> <strong>loading</strong> images wil=
l be loaded not before the user scrolls near them ("lazy" - better performa=
nce!) or immediately on loading the page. If not set explicitly, "lazy" is =
used.</div>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>

</div>

<h3 class=3D"sectionedit10" id=3D"videos">Videos</h3>
<div class=3D"level3">
<ul>
<li class=3D"level1 node"><div class=3D"li"> [video=3D"VIDEOPATH" (width=3D=
"N") (height=3D"N") (float=3D"left"|"right")] <br>
<em>(items in parenthesis are optional, when you use those items you have t=
o leave away the parenthesis!))</em>.</div>
<ul>
<li class=3D"level2 node"><div class=3D"li"> <strong>VIDEOPATH</strong> may=
 be:</div>
<ul>
<li class=3D"level3"><div class=3D"li"> an uploaded file: "attachs/video.mp=
4"</div>
</li>
<li class=3D"level3"><div class=3D"li"> a remote file: "https//example.org/=
video.mp4"</div>
</li>
<li class=3D"level3"><div class=3D"li"> a YouTube link: "https://www.youtub=
e.com/watch?v=3DTHEVIDEO"</div>
</li>
<li class=3D"level3"><div class=3D"li"> a Facebook Video link: "https://www=
.facebook.com/watch/?v=3DTHEVIDEO"</div>
</li>
<li class=3D"level3"><div class=3D"li"> a Vimeo link: "https://vimeo.com/TH=
EVIDEO"</div>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li class=3D"level2"><div class=3D"li"> <strong>width</strong> and <strong>=
height</strong> set the width or height on the video in pixels. You can use=
